        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the following properties to explain how they are used with TrustedTypes:</p>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/innerHTML\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Element.innerHTML</code> </a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is in progress:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Addd boilerplate</li>\n<li>Add links to recommended alternatives - really you should use setHTML.</li>\n<li>Add TT information, including the new exception</li>\n<li>Restructured - this isn't to current templates. Need to move the guidish stuff either down as examples or up into description</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Still looking at the examples and structure. I expect next to make them all use TT by default.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2770544982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\">#37518</a> (tracking issue)</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40423",
            "title": "Element.innerHTML - add info trusted types",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-18T07:06:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-18T07:04:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the following methods to explain how they are used with TrustedTypes:</p>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/parseHTMLUnsafe_static\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Document.parseHTMLUnsafe()</code> </a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/setHTMLUnsafe\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Element.setHTMLUnsafe()</code> </a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ShadowRoot/setHTMLUnsafe\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot.setHTMLUnsafe()</code> </a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Initially I have just subedited a little and added the (not-quite-right) boilerplate from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2829390584\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37952\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/37952/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/37952\">#37952</a>. This is mostly to create a environment for working out where to go moving forward.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2770544982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\">#37518</a> (tracking issue)</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These methods are tricky because the standard boilerplate recommending using trusted HTML is not true, or at least not reasonable to follow:</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"></path></svg>Warning</p><p dir=\"auto\">This API parses its input as HTML, writing the result into the DOM.<br>\nAPIs like this are known as <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Trusted_Types_API#concepts_and_usage\">injection sinks</a>, and are potentially a vector for <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Attacks/XSS\">cross-site-scripting (XSS)</a> attacks, if the input originally came from an attacker.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For this reason it's much safer to pass only {{domxref(\"TrustedHTML\")}} objects into this method, and to <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Trusted_Types_API#using_a_csp_to_enforce_trusted_types\">enforce</a> this using the <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/require-trusted-types-for\"><code class=\"notranslate\">require-trusted-types-for</code></a> CSP directive.<br>\nThis means you can be sure that the input has been passed through a transformation function, which has the chance to <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Attacks/XSS#sanitization\">sanitize</a> the input to remove potentially dangerous markup, such as {{htmlelement(\"script\")}} elements and event handler attributes.</p>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The reason is that these methods take a sanitizer argument that can inject the input string in a context-aware way. You could use the transform but you would be better off using this sanitizer, and you wouldn't do both. So why do we need TT in this case, and what would it look like.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The simplistic answer is probably that if we're enforcing TTs then we'll need to pass at TT or have a default TT or this will fail. So for this case the simple answer would be \"you don't need to do anything special but you should create an unsafeSanitizedHTML policy and use that for all these APIs. In other words it isn't useful.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to make it useful. I played with prompting ChatGPT to generate code that achieves the goal of TT, which is to ensure that all code is audited, and that auditing is in a known place. It didn't really use TT for this, but it did come up with the idea of <code class=\"notranslate\">safeParseHTML()</code> which wraps the method with something that ensures you always pass the required policy, and ensures that your sanitizer is always one that is \"registered/trusted\".</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const approvedSanitizers = new WeakSet();\n\nfunction registerSanitizer(fn) {\n  approvedSanitizers.add(fn);\n  return fn;\n}\n\nconst parsePolicy = trustedTypes.createPolicy('parseHTMLPolicy', {\n  createHTML(input) {\n    // Developer must pass input through here manually\n    return input;\n  }\n});\n\nfunction safeParseHTML(rawInput, sanitizer) {\n  if (!approvedSanitizers.has(sanitizer)) {\n    throw new TypeError('Unapproved sanitizer passed to safeParseHTML');\n  }\n\n  const trusted = parsePolicy.createHTML(rawInput);\n  return parseHTMLUnsafe(trusted, sanitizer);\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">approvedSanitizers</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">WeakSet</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">registerSanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">fn</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-s1\">approvedSanitizers</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">add</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">fn</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">fn</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">parsePolicy</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">trustedTypes</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">createPolicy</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'parseHTMLPolicy'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">createHTML</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">input</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\">// Developer must pass input through here manually</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">input</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">safeParseHTML</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">rawInput</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">!</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">approvedSanitizers</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">has</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">sanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">throw</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">TypeError</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'Unapproved sanitizer passed to safeParseHTML'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">trusted</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">parsePolicy</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">createHTML</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">rawInput</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">parseHTMLUnsafe</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">trusted</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const mySanitizer = registerSanitizer(\n  new HTMLSanitizer({ allowElements: ['b', 'i', 'a'] })\n);\n\nsafeParseHTML('&lt;b&gt;hello&lt;/b&gt;', mySanitizer);\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">mySanitizer</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">registerSanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">HTMLSanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">allowElements</span>: <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'b'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'i'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'a'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-en\">safeParseHTML</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'&lt;b&gt;hello&lt;/b&gt;'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">mySanitizer</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/wbamberg/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/wbamberg\">@wbamberg</a> <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/lukewarlow/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/lukewarlow\">@lukewarlow</a> Would love your thoughts on how this API should be used with trusted types.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40420",
            "title": "TrustedTypes: Add boilerplate for the xxxHtmlUnsafe() methods",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-19T11:06:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-18T02:47:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
