        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43580235?u=cae42d5a371dd041072ce6d85a1808de05535be8&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Small migration of embedgh sample into the page.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's easier to maintain this way.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40413",
            "title": "chore: move EmbedGH live sample into the page",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-18T16:15:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-17T15:03:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bsmth",
                "url": "https://github.com/bsmth"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome has added several <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FedCM_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">FedCM</a> features that we are missing from MDN. This PR adds docs for them.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The features are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Support for multiple IdPs in a single <code class=\"notranslate\">get()</code> call, as specified inside the <code class=\"notranslate\">providers</code> array, added in Chrome 136: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5067784766095360\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5067784766095360</a></li>\n<li>The above ChromeStatus entry also includes the <code class=\"notranslate\">IdentityCredential.configURL</code> (if you look at the <a href=\"https://github.com/w3c-fedid/FedCM/pull/686/files#diff-40cc3a1ba233cc3ca7b6d5873260da9676f6ae20bb897b62f7871c80d0bda4e9R445\">associated spec changes</a>)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">IdentityCredential.disconnect()</code>, added in Chrome 122: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5202286040580096\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5202286040580096</a>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">identity.mode</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">get()</code> calls, added in Chrome 132: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4689551782313984\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/4689551782313984</a>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">identity.fields</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">identity.params</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">get()</code> calls, added in Chrome 132. I'm not sure what ChromeStatus entry covers these, but <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/cookies/fedcm/implement/relying-party#providers_property\" rel=\"nofollow\">developer.chrome.com</a> says they were added in Chrome 132.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">account_label</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">label_hints</code> in the IdP config file / accounts list endpoint. This was added in Chrome 132. Note that this won't have browser compat data - we don't really have a way of recording data for features in endpoints related to an API.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">supports_use_other_account</code> in the IdP config file.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">domain_hints</code> in the accounts list endpoint and <code class=\"notranslate\">domainHint</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">get()</code> calls.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One point I'd especially like the tech review to comment on — the specified <a href=\"https://w3c-fedid.github.io/FedCM/#dictdef-identitycredentialdisconnectoptions\" rel=\"nofollow\">options object for <code class=\"notranslate\">disconnect()</code></a> does not match up with the description in the <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/cookies/fedcm/implement/relying-party#disconnect_the_idp_from_the_rp\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome docs</a>. I think the latter makes more sense, but I'd like to know what is going on here.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40411",
            "title": "Technical review: Document recent FedCM additions, Chrome 122-136",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-19T13:37:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-17T13:54:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Almost finishing <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1237891052\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/16120\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/16120/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/16120\">#16120</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm having a really hard time coming up with convincing examples, because the existing ones surely don't convince me. <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pepelsbey/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pepelsbey\">@pepelsbey</a> pointed me to the new Fred architecture which is helpful. I'm also pointing to another internal example for reference.</p>",
